================================================================================
Mutable Instruments Plaits -- MIT
================================================================================

The MicroFreak's Speech engine is Mutable Instruments' Plaits LPC speech
synthesiser. This was established by byte-exact comparison against
`pichenettes/eurorack`, not by inference: the 14-byte frame struct, the
15-entry phoneme table, the quantisation lookup tables, the 640-entry
excitation pulse, and the word banks all match the published MIT source
value for value. See `docs/SPEECH.md` for the evidence.

Because that upstream source is MIT, the tables in this repository are
redistributable under the terms below. They are Emilie Gillet's work, not
Arturia's and not this project's.

No Plaits-derived code is in THIS repository. The quantisation tables, the
bitstream layout and the excitation pulse are in the sibling project
microfreak-tools (`microfreak/lpc.py`, `plugins/speech/mfreak_speech/render.py`),
whose own NOTICE carries this attribution for them.

What is here is `docs/SPEECH.md`, which documents the correspondence:
which Plaits structure each piece of the MicroFreak's Speech engine matches,
and how that was established. It describes published source rather than
reproducing it. The notice below is reproduced because that document quotes
the structures it identifies, and because the credit is owed either way.

